  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian assistance South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian assitance in South Sudan- WASH and reduced vulnerability
.
Impact: Save lives, alleviate suffering and protect human dignity in humanitarian crises 

Outcomes: WASH and reduced vulnerability. 
WASH activities include distribution of hygiene kits, women and girls receiving sanitary kits, WASH awareness raising sessions and access to basic drinking water services through rehabilitation of boreholes. 
Reduced vulnerability activities include: distribution of vegetable seeds, training on recommended agronomic practices, women will be organised into VSLAs, 9 payam level peace committees will be established, as well as 9 payam level community action groups (CAGs). 4 trainings for partner staff and volunteers will be conducted on safeguarding, CHS and other thematic areas.

The project will target specifically vulnerable groups such as Persons Living with Disabilities,
Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) and women.</narrative>
  </description>
